/tmp/paper_2212_02272/src/arXivMain.tex:361:In this paper, we study an analogue of this conjecture for digraphs. For a digraph $D$ we denote by $\omega(D)$ the clique number of the underlying graph of $D$ and by $\dic(D)$ its {\em dichromatic number}, that is the minimum integer $k$ such that the set of vertices of $D$ can be partitioned into $k$ acyclic subdigraphs. A class of digraphs $\mC$ is $\dic$-bounded if there exists a function $f$ such that every digraph $D$ in $\mC$ satisfies $\dic(D)\leq f(\omega(D))$. 
