The exact paper regime is now clear: loopless oriented graphs (no antiparallel arcs), “triangle-free” means the underlying graph has clique number at most 2, and the forbidden \(P_6\) is an induced directed path. The main theorem only guarantees a 382-dicolouring; its proof is structural, not a hardness result. I’m therefore testing a Track B family built around the paper’s native odd-directed-cycle object from Lemma 3, with a linear mechanical search and a short algebraic composition route.
