The script reported `cap_bound` only because the shifted ladder kept `mask_pairs=24` constant, so its per-run detector saw one moving axis and could not know the immediately preceding run had already swept 8→24 pairs. I’m correcting the ladder metadata—not adding new hardness—so the final audit visibly moves both fixed-length axes in one transcript. This avoids a false park and lets the harness issue the appropriate `too_easy` verdict if the same solved levels repeat.
